  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math><br />i.e.&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/846c6b61-9c3a-4699-a0b8-58c380a00218.jpeg\" /><br />Using perpendicular distance of line from origin, minimum value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math><br />Maximum value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />So,&nbsp;<math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> can&rsquo;t be <math><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt></math></p>",
